2026-11-25T06:41:39 | Claude sandbox builder | found | sbx v0.53.0 runs on this Windows 11 Home (diagnose: hypervisor present). Trial results on a scratch sandbox: (1) nested read-only extra workspaces work: `sbx create claude <proj> <proj>\\secret:ro <proj>\\.git:ro` makes secret/ and .git/ readable but every create/change/delete fails with "Read-only file system", also as root via sudo and after a remount attempt (host-enforced). (2) Network: with `sbx policy init deny-all` the claude kit still allows api.anthropic.com, claude.com, platform.claude.com, downloads.claude.ai, mcp-proxy..., deb.debian.org; claude.ai (needed for login) is NOT allowed and must be added per sandbox; example.com/github.com are blocked, DNS lookups blocked. (3) host.docker.internal:7431/health answers from inside once `localhost:7431` is allowed (host Kestrel on 127.0.0.1 IS reachable); but the better route is the sbx MCP gateway: the board registered with `sbx mcp add --url http://127.0.0.1:7431/mcp` + header secret keeps the token on the host, never in the sandbox; initialize through the gateway returned the board's instructions. (4) `ssh <name>.sbx` works after `sbx settings set feature.ssh true` + daemon restart. (5) Agent has passwordless sudo and docker group in the stock image; the template will drop both.
